course: dictionary
lesson: 6600
title: Noisy and what it can mean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Noisy means making a lot of loud sound. A noisy class is one where many children are talking and shouting at once. «Each chick has its own voice, and its parents recognise it among thousands of others in a noisy colony.» Here noisy describes a place full of loud sounds.
explain: Noisy has a second meaning in science and data. There it means full of random, unwanted bits that make it hard to see what is going on. In class, a teacher might say «you're too noisy» to ask for quiet, so the word can also be a request for less sound.
explain: Noisy changes to show more or most: noisy, noisier, noisiest. A road is noisier than a park. A busy motorway is often the noisiest place of all. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if the sentence still makes sense, you have found it.
fact: Noisy means making a lot of loud sound.
fact: A noisy place is full of loud sounds, like a busy street.
fact: In science, noise is measured in decibels, and very noisy places can damage hearing.
fact: Ear defenders protect your ears from very loud noise.
fact: The comparing forms are noisier and noisiest.
exercise: «Each chick has its own voice, and its parents recognise it among thousands of others in a noisy colony.» What does noisy describe here? | A shy, quiet bird | *A place full of loud sounds | A tasty meal for the parents | A cold, empty nest
exercise: Your teacher says, «You're too noisy.» What does she want? | A song | Louder talking | *Quiet | A new seat by the window
exercise: Finish the sentence: The road is ___ than the park. | noisy | *noisier | noisiest | noise
test: «Being noisy at funerals and memorials can hurt grieving people for a long time.» What does noisy mean here? | Bright and shiny | Quiet and calm | Sad and tired | *Making a lot of loud sound
test: In a noisy place like a road, why should you look carefully? | Cars make no sound at all | Noise makes cars drive slower | *You might not hear a car coming | Roads are always empty
exam: In science and data, what can noisy mean? | A bright, shiny surface | Making a lot of loud sound in a class | *Full of random, unwanted bits that make it hard to see what is going on | Very old and broken
